CPU-side steady clock; nanoseconds per retired record averaged over a block of 1024 updates.
Per distribution: 64 warmup blocks discarded, 512 measured blocks; nearest-rank p50/p95/p99.
No GL calls, driver polling, CSV, rendering, or fake timestamp values are timed.
The mixed stream delivers one adjacent pair out of order per 32 records. The baseline checksum follows the last arrival; the fix follows the greatest originating frame.
